No. 7 · The Roman Dodecahedron — credits

Made in code, in three worlds: Archive Room, Orbit and Studio 3D (after styles from Lemo-Opuscar by Lemomo,
https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT / CC BY 4.0). No generated imagery, no stock footage.

Objects and documents (Archive Room)
- Roman dodecahedron, Tongeren (Leopoldwal, 1939), Gallo-Roman Museum Tongeren inv. 4002. Photo: Gallo-Roman Museum Tongeren, via Wikimedia Commons, CC0 1.0. (The white backdrop seen through its holes is made transparent.)
- Vitruvius, De architectura (Como, 1521), table of chapters; Library of Congress NA2515 .V8 1521, public domain.
- Vegetius, De re militari (1475), Library of Congress Incun. X .V37, public domain.
- Apicius, De re coquinaria (1498), Library of Congress Incun. 1498 .A6, public domain.
- Wall painting from Room L of the Villa of P. Fannius Synistor at Boscoreale, c. 50–40 BC. The Metropolitan Museum of Art 03.14.4, Rogers Fund, 1903, Open Access (CC0).
- Marble relief fragment depicting athletic prizes, 2nd c. AD. The Metropolitan Museum of Art 59.11.19, Rogers Fund, 1959, Open Access (CC0).
- Sestertii of Trajan (08.170.121) and Titus (08.170.117), Rogers Fund, 1908; sestertius of Trebonianus Gallus (05.47), Gift of William M. Laffan, 1905. The Metropolitan Museum of Art, Open Access (CC0).
- Hunt Museum catalogue description of HCM 157, via Europeana (record 325/HCM157, metadata CC0), transcribed onto a card.
- Much Hadham find, Portable Antiquities Scheme 941889: figures from its record as quoted on Wikimedia Commons.

Places (Orbit)
- NASA Blue Marble (shaded relief and bathymetry), via NASA GIBS, public domain.
- Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016 by EOX IT Services GmbH (https://s2maps.eu), CC BY 4.0; contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2016.
- Country outlines: Natural Earth 1:50m, public domain.

Studio 3D
- The dodecahedra, golf ball, rule, candle and yarn are 3D reconstructions built in code (three.js); the main model uses the
  recorded size and hole range of the Much Hadham find (82 mm, holes 13.7–20 mm). Marked "3D RECONSTRUCTION" on screen.

Surfaces, lights, props
- Poly Haven (CC0): wood_table_worn, velour_velvet, red_plaster_weathered, farm_soil textures; desk_lamp_arm_01 model;
  photo_studio_loft_hall and lythwood_lounge HDRIs.

